MCP usage:
1. Claude integration
https://opentools.com/registry/markitdown    //convert docs to markdown
open a folder in VScode, run:
$ python3 -m venv venv
$ source venv/bin/activate
$ pip install markitdown-mcp
$ markitdown-mcp --http --host 127.0.0.1 --port 3001
Claude -> Add custom connector, then fill in 'Convert to Markdown' and 'http://127.0.0.1:3001'
then found the same issue: https://github.com/anthropics/claude-ai-mcp/issues/9
solved in this way: using pre-built docker image instead of python package
added in claude_desktop_config.json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "markitdown": {
      "command": "podman",
      "args": [
        "run",
        "--rm",
        "-i",
        "mcp/markitdown:latest"
      ]
    }
  },
}
in terminal:
$ podman ps
$ podman machine ls
$ podman machine start
$ podman pull mcp/markitdown                  //https://hub.docker.com/r/mcp/markitdown
$ podman images
open Claude -> Connectors, markitdown should be enabled there. 
upload a file and input "please convert this file to markdown", it should work.



